{
  "year": 2022,
  "pointsSystem": "2022 CrossFit Games individual scoring on a 100-point-per-event scale, using TWO tables because the field was cut once mid-competition (40->30 after Saturday's events, before the Sunday final day; this was the only mid-competition cut, per the official announcement games.crossfit.com/announcement/13704). Events 2022-01 through 2022-11 (40-athlete field) use the 40-athlete table: places 1-20 score 100, 97, 94, ... descending by 3 (1st=100, 5th=88, 10th=73, 15th=58, 20th=43); places 21-40 then descend by 2 (21st=40, 30th=22, 39th=4, 40th=2). Events 2022-12, 2022-13 and 2022-14 (Sunday, contested by the 30 remaining athletes) use the 30-athlete table: places 1-13 descend by 4 (1st=100, 2nd=96, 3rd=92, 4th=88, 5th=84, ... 13th=52), then places 14-30 descend by 3 (14th=49, 15th=46, ... 30th=1). First place is worth 100 on both tables. Thirteen named tests produced 14 scored events because Shuttle to Overhead was split into two 100-point scores (2A run time = event 2022-04, 2B max jerks = event 2022-05), so the maximum possible total was 1,400 points (a win in all 14 events). Final placement determined by total points across all 14 events. The Skill Speed Medley (2022-02) was a placement-only elimination race; the leaderboard records its score as the athlete's event rank (e.g. '1 pt').",
